From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:28:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 70/93] usb: dwc3: apple: T6050's sleep lines where the sleep
 is described

The dwc3 glue took T6050's sleep lines on the J714s and the J716c by
name. Take them wherever the device tree describes T6050's sleep.

The port controllers' side of this is in already: their sleep rules are
asked for by the controllers' own properties.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>

[re-cut onto the K114s r3d tree]
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
index c5740ee25d5..5757cf33832 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
@@ -1109,12 +1109,12 @@ static void dwc3_apple_check_hub_later(struct dwc3_apple *appledwc)
 
 /*
  * Waiting for a Type-C PHY that is not started after sleep is specific to the T6050 boards
- * whose port controllers take the sleep's power states (J714s, J716c). The notifier work
- * and its admission rules apply to every board.
+ * whose port controllers take the sleep's power states: those whose device tree describes
+ * the sleep. The notifier work and its admission rules apply to every board.
  */
 static bool dwc3_apple_sleep_board(void)
 {
-	return of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j714s") || of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j716c");
+	return apple_t6050_sleep_described();
 }
 
